   "he": "כֹּהֵן אוֹכֵל בְּקׇדְשֵׁי קֳדָשִׁים, דִּכְתִיב: ״כׇּל זָכָר בִּבְנֵי אַהֲרֹן יֹאכֲלֶנָּה״.",
   "en": "The mishna states: «A priest may eat from offerings of the most sacred order,» but a daughter of a priest may not eat from offerings of the most sacred order. The Gemara explains: This is derived «as it is written» with regard to the meal-offering, which is an offering of the most sacred order: «“Every male among the children of Aaron may eat of it”» (Leviticus 6:11)."
  }
